"""The evaluation runner (Sections 10-12): every system variant on the benchmark's queries, the
metrics in eval/schema.py's results.csv, an LLM judge for naturalness checked against human
ratings, paired statistics against the full system, and a cost estimate with a spending cap.

Variants (`evaluation.variants` in config.yaml) switch one thing at a time:
- the architecture: the four-agent graph, or one LLM call (`single_agent`) that sees every
  listing with the same tool outputs (market price for its condition, scam risk and red flags,
  landed cost, seller signals) and must pick and answer in one pass;
- the model: the small model (plan ablation 5) or the frontier model in one pass (ablation 6);
- one component: reflection (price and scam checks, ablation 3), red-flag retrieval, the
  clarifying question, the number check, the LLM reply (template only), memory, the scoring.

`python -m src.evaluation run --variants full,single_agent --split dev` writes
eval/results/<time>_<label>/: results.csv (one row per query, variant and repeat),
replies.jsonl (each reply and what was picked) and run.json. Then `judge`, `stats` and
`estimate` read that folder. Repeats are part of the LLM cache key: repeat 0, 1 and 2 are real
calls, and running the same repeat again is free (but its latency is then meaningless, so
cached calls are counted in every row).
"""

